  <p>
    corrected and uncorrected. A corrected item-scale correlation compares an item to all the remaining items in the scale, excluding itself. In an uncorrected item-scale correlation, the item of interest is left in the scale to which it is compared.
  </p>

  <h3 style="margin-top: 20px;">A. Corrected item-scale correlations</h3>
  <p>
    The correlation matrix (see below, Table 2: Correlation Matrix for Corrected Scale) shows the correlations between a scale item and the remaining items in the scale.
  </p>
  <p>
    There are three significant values in the corrected item-scale correlations, and only two are in the expected direction. The results for this criterion indicate low reliability.
  </p>

